	abstract = {This paper is an effort to develop an FPGA coprocessor to off-load intensive computing tasks associated with electromagnetic transient simulation, allowing the simulation to be performed in real-time. A sample singlephase test system was used to examine the principle. The equivalent is implemented and simulated using Xilinx ISE 4.2 and ModelSim simulator. The results show that FPGA technology offers a cheap alternative for real-time applications},
